# mina.vn - a layered PSD character (masters/char/mina.psd) with a hand-written rig (assets/char/mina/rig.json).
# Nothing jumps here: put the cursor on a line below and use Preview from cursor (Ctrl+Enter).
# Open her rig from the Files panel (Characters) or Ctrl+P, then #.

define mina "Mina" color=#b48cff

label mina_demo:
  scene bg_park_evening fade 0.5
  show mina at center fade 0.4
  mina: This is a layered PSD character. Eyes, mouth and the two outfit parts are slots; the rest are plain parts. #p2r0

  # A pose from the PSD: picks, per slot, the variant named or aliased "smile" (eyes and mouth here).
  show mina smile
  mina: "smile" is a PSD variant name, so it works without any rig.json. #dryj

  # One slot by name: slot=variant. The line beats whatever a pose picked.
  show mina eyes=closed
  mina: slot=variant overrides a single slot. #xhdd

  # A look (rig.json "looks"): a map from slots to variants under one name.
  show mina uniform
  mina: "uniform" sets both top and bottom to school. #od2v
  show mina shy
  mina: "shy" is the smile look with a neutral mouth. #rdgs
  show mina casual
  mina: "casual" is the happy look and the casual outfit in one word. #rbq9

  # Several looks on one line apply left to right: the last one wins per slot.
  show mina casual uniform
  mina: Casual first, then uniform, so the uniform wins. #bm9q

  # A line wins over a look: casual, but the mouth open.
  show mina casual mouth=open
  mina: Explicit slot=variant after a look wins over what it set. #mv0y

  # rig.json "animations": keyframes of your own, played with `animate`.
  mina: Keyframe animations live in rig.json too. #zz01
  animate mina wave
  animate mina giggle loop
  mina: This one loops until it is stopped. #zz02
  animate mina stop

  # rig.json "order" re-stacks parts: top is drawn over bottom, so the shirt hangs over the skirt (see the rig).
  show mina uniform
  hide mina fade 0.4
  end
